{
 "9101": {
  "en": [
   "Today, who are those heard weeping — where do the orphaned cry alas, alas,",
   "Days and months pass, the year runs out — will the wailing never end?",
   "Who are those gazing with vacant eyes toward a new year without joy or hope,",
   "Who lie on the parched bed of earth — desert on every side.",
   "Speaking words of assurance to all, the year had come bearing so many hopes,",
   "Trampling so many hopes it departs today — how many homes left empty.",
   "It wiped away so many wretches' means of living, leaving tears behind —",
   "On the rising path of the new year it left darkness behind.",
   "Alas, will one whose home holds not a grain of food not receive even human love —",
   "Are there today no streams of pity's tears for the afflicted?",
   "Weep and say, 'Lord, let sorrow depart, let the scorched earth's heart be soothed —",
   "if the year must go, let it take with it the year's burden of grief.'"
  ],
