 "9105": {
  "en": [
   "You, O sun of love, lighting all creation,",
   "however much you bestow, undiminished is your hand.",
   "Stay shining upon the eyes of these two —",
   "then tell me, what is there to fear from the dark?",
   "If they lose you, the two will lose each other —",
   "the two will sit and weep, blinded in dense delusion;",
   "such darkness will fall that, seated side by side,",
   "still the two will not know each other's faces.",
   "See, Lord, stay awake upon their eyes for ever —",
   "let not the world's dense clouds cover you.",
   "Seated in your light, their moon-faces bright,",
   "each beholds the other, their whole being athrill."
  ],
